  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">SECURING THE GREATER NORTH LUANGWA LANDSCAPE FOR THE PROTECTION OF AFRICAN ELEPHANTS IN THE LUANGWA VALLEY, ZAMBIA</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">THE PURPOSE OF THIS PROJECT IS TO SUPPORT AN ELEPHANT CONSERVATION EFFORT IN ZAMBIA S NORTH LUANGWA NATIONAL PARK (NLNP) AND SURROUNDING GAME MANAGEMENT AREAS BY STRENGTHENING ELEPHANT PROTECTION AND BIOLOGICAL MONITORING AND ENHANCING HUMAN-ELEPHANT COEXISTENCE. AS PART OF THE LUANGWA-ZAMBEZI VALLEY SAVANNA ELEPHANT STRONGHOLD, THIS ECOSYSTEM IS HOME TO ZAMBIAS LARGEST POPULATION OF ELEPHANTS, WITH APPROXIMATELY 20,000 INDIVIDUALS. THIS PROJECT IS INTENDED TO CONSERVE AFRICAN SAVANNA ELEPHANTS AND THEIR HABITAT BY ADDRESSING THE IMPACTS OF POACHING AND HUMAN-ELEPHANT CONFLICT (HEC). SPECIFIC ACTIVITIES INCLUDE: (1) PROVIDING ADEQUATE RATIONS (3,300 FIELD RATION PACKS) FOR EXTENDED ANTI-POACHING PATROLS (2) REFURBISHING THE PROJECTS HUSKY AIRCRAFT ENGINE TO SUPPORT SUSTAINED AND SAFE AERIAL MONITORING OPERATIONS AND (3) PROVISIONING OF TWO NEW VEHICLES AND FUEL (345,000 LITERS) FOR GAME MANAGEMENT AREA CONSERVATION FIELD ACTIVITIES, INCLUDING RESPONSE TO HUMAN-WILDLIFE CONFLICT INCIDENTS.</narrative>
  </description>
